#statement("Definition")[
$X arrow.r^f Y$ is a #strong[weak homotopy equivalence]#index-entry("Weak homotopy equivalence") if $pi_0\(X\,x_0\)arrow.r^(f_(*)) pi_0\(Y\,f\(x_0\)\)$ is bijective, and on each path connected component, $pi_n\(X\,x_0\)arrow.r^(f_(*)) pi_n\(Y\,f\(x_0\)\)$ are isomorphisms

]
#statement("Theorem", title: [Hurewicz theorem])[
Choose a generator $e in H_n\(S^n\)$, define $phi.alt : pi_n\(X\)arrow.r H_n\(X\)$, $f mapsto f_(*)\(e\)$, here $f : S^n arrow.r X$ is a map. If $X$ is $\(n - 1\)$-connected, then $phi.alt$ is an isomorphism

]#label("Hurewicz theorem")
