#statement("Lemma")[
If $X times { 0 } union A times I$ is a retract of $X times I$, then the topology of the mapping cylinder of the inclusion $A arrow.r.hook X$ is the the same as the subspace topology on $X times { 0 } union A times I$ induced from $X times I$. In particular, $f$ is continuous on $X times { 0 } union A times I$ iff $f$ is continuous on both $X times { 0 }$ and $A times I$

]#label("Mapping cylinder of inclusion has subspace topology if it is a retraction")
#proof(title: "Proof")[
This is trivial if $A$ is closed due to Lemma #ref(label("Pasting lemma"), supplement: none)

Write $Y = X times { 0 } union A times I$. If $O subset.eq Y$ is open in $Y$, then obviously $O inter A times I$ is open in $A times I$, $O inter X$ is open in $X$

Suppose $O subset.eq Y$ is such that $O inter A times I$ is open in $A times I$, $O inter X$ is open in $X$. Define $U_n = union.big_V {V subset.eq^(upright(o p e n)) X mid(bar.v) \( V inter A \) times \[ 0 \, 1 / n \) subset.eq O}$, i.e. $U_n$ is the largest such open subset of $X$, $U = union.big_(n = 1)^oo U_n$, then $O inter A subset.eq U$ since for any $\(x\,0\)in O inter A subset.eq O inter A times I$, because $O inter A times I$ is open $A times I$, there exists open subset $V subset.eq X$ containing $x$ such that $\(V inter A\)times\[0\,1 / n\)subset.eq O inter A times I$ for some $n$, hence $x in V subset.eq U_n subset.eq U$

$O inter A times\(0\,1\]$ is open in $Y$, $O inter\(X\\overline(A)\)$ is open in $Y$, we only need to show that for any $x in overline(A)$, there exists an open neighborhood of $\(x\,0\)$ contained in $O$, and it suffices to show that $x in U$, then $x in U_n$ for some $n$, $\(U_n inter O\)times\[0\,1 / n\)inter Y$ is open in $Y$. Now fix $x in overline(A)$

Write the retraction $r$ as $\(r_1\,r_2\)$, for $t > 0$, $r\(x\,t\)=\(r_1\(x\,t\)\,r_2\(x\,t\)\)$, since $x in overline(A)$, $r\(a\,t\)=\(a\,t\)$, we know $r_1\(x\,t\)in A$, $r_2\(x\,t\)= t$. We claim: if $r_1\(x\,t\)in U_n$, then $x in U_n$. Since $U_n$ is open, there exists open neighborhood $V$ of $x$ such that $r_1\(V times\(t - epsilon\,t + epsilon\)\)subset.eq U_n$ for some $epsilon > 0$, in particular $r_1\(\(V inter A\)times { t }\)subset.eq U_n$, thus $V inter A subset.eq U_n inter A$, by maximality of $U_n$, $V subset.eq U_n$

Suppose $x in.not U$, then by the claim, $r_1\(x\,t\)in A\\U$ for $t > 0$, then $r_1\(x\,t\)in A\\O$ since $A inter O subset.eq U$, thus $x = r_1\(x\,0\)in overline(A)\\O$ which contradicts the fact $\(x\,0\)in A$

]
#statement("Proposition")[
$\(X\,A\)$ is cofibered iff $X times { 0 } union A times I$ is a retract of $X times I$ iff $X times { 0 } union A times I$ is a strong deformation retract of $X times I$

]#label("A->X is a cofibration iff retraction exists")
#proof(title: "Proof")[
If $A arrow.r^i X$ is a cofibration, then $X times { 0 } union A times I arrow.r^1 X times { 0 } union A times I$ induces a retraction. Conversely, by Lemma #ref(label("Mapping cylinder of inclusion has subspace topology if it is a retraction"), supplement: none), $A times I arrow.r^g Y$, $X arrow.r^(f_0) Y$ with $g_0 = f_0\|_A$ gives a map $X times { 0 } union A times I arrow.r Y$, composing with retraction gives $X times I arrow.r Y$

A strong deformation retraction is given by $H\(\(x\,t\)\,s\)=\(Pr_X r\(x\,s t\)\,s Pr_I r\(x\,t\)+\(1 - s\)t\)$

]
