#statement("Proposition")[
If $\(X\,A\)$, $\(Y\,B\)$ are cofibered, $A subset.eq X$ is closed, then $\(X times Y\,X times B union A times Y\)$ is also cofibered. If in addition $A$ or $B$ is a strong deformation retract of $X$ or $Y$, then $X times B union A times Y$ is a strong deformation retract of $X times Y$

]
#statement("Proposition")[
$E arrow.r^p B$ is a fibration, then the fibers over connected components of $B$ are homotopic. More over, for any path $gamma : I arrow.r B$, we can get a lifting $g_t : F_(gamma\(0\)) arrow.r F_(gamma\(t\))$ of $F_(gamma\(0\)) arrow.r.hook E$, define $L_gamma : F_(gamma\(0\)) arrow.r F_(gamma\(1\))$ to be $g_1$, if $gamma tilde.eq eta$ rel $partial I : I arrow.r B$, then $L_gamma tilde.eq L_eta$, and for any $gamma\,eta : I arrow.r B$, $eta\(0\)= gamma\(1\)$, $L_(gamma eta) tilde.eq L_gamma L_eta$

]#label("Fibers of fibration are homotopy equivalent")
#proof(title: "Proof")[
According to homotopy lifting property, lifting up $A times F_(gamma\(0\)) arrow.r E$ is homeomorphic to $B times F_(gamma\(0\)) arrow.r E$

]
#aside("Remark")[
