#statement("Lemma")[
Cofibration $A arrow.r^i X$ is a homotopy equivalence iff $A$ is a strong deformation retract of $X$. Fibration $E arrow.r^p B$ is a homotopy equivalence iff there exists a section $B arrow.r^s E$ such that $s p$ is fiber homotopic to $1$

]#label("i:A->B cofibration is homotopy equivalence iff A strong deformation retract")
#proof(title: "Proof")[
If $i$ is a homotopy equivalence, then there exists $X arrow.r^(r') A$ such that $i r' tilde.eq 1_X$, $r' i tilde.eq 1_A$, by Lemma #ref(label("Some rudimentary lemma about retract and deformation"), supplement: none), since $\(X\,A\)$ is cofibered, $r' tilde.eq r$ is a retract and then $A$ is a deformation retract of $X$. Suppose $X times I arrow.r^F X$ is a homotopy from $1_X$ to $i r$

$Gamma = X times { 0 } union A times I union X times { 1 } = X times { 0 } union A times\[0\,1 / 2\]union A times\[1 / 2\,1\]union X times { 1 }$ is a retract of $X times I$. Construct $Gamma times I arrow.r^G X$ #display-equation($G\(\(x\,t\)\,s\)= cases(F\(x\,\(1 - s\)t\)quad\(x\,t\)in X times { 0 } union A times I, F\(r\(x\)\,1 - s\)quad\(x\,t\)in X times { 1 })$) $G_1$ can be extends to $X times I arrow.r^H X$, then $H_0\(x\)= G_1\(x\,0\)= F\(x\,0\)= x$, $H_1\(x\)= G_1\(x\,1\)= F\(r\(x\)\,0\)= r\(x\)$, $H_t\(a\)= G_1\(a\,t\)= F\(a\,0\)= a$, i.e. $H$ is a strong deformation retraction

]
#statement("Lemma")[
